{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers","id":1219327,"title":"Supernatural Consors (retainers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-16T11:43:15-07:00","id":1219327,"title":"Supernatural Consors (retainers)","content":"As Gods &amp; Monsters book is still somewhere on the horizon I wanted to ask what sort of beings would you consider as supernatural companions. The game gives us a version of Vampire/Werewolf companions and some bygones. Though, got to admit that samples given are limited and thus not very exciting. <br /> <br /> \u200bSo, please write about what fictional things/beings you would consider for mage companion/friends and for how many merit points. Character sheets are welcome, as well as background details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:04:05-07:00","id":1219408,"title":"","content":"Right now, the Templar PC in the game has a black lab familiar that is fitting the Comes Celestias (Divine Companions) from the Book of Crafts. This is a former bomb dog which is inhabited by an angelic spirit. I use the standard large dog M20 template and the spirit inhabiting the dog body, possesses some knowledge of Christian theology and mysticism. It also has Demolitions and Unconventional Warfare to reflect being a bomb dog working for the U.S. military in Afghanistan. I figure about 2 dots in all the special knowledges, plus regular dog skills and abilities. Once in a while, God talks to the angel inside the dog as well. . . The attached PC is a military veteran who Awakened during a roadside IED incident that wiped out her squad.<br /> <br /> I'd love to have a faerie dragon consor for one NPC, but it doesn't work so well in a modern game. Most of the bygones are going to work better in areas where the Consensus is not in force and the reality zone does not favor the Technocracy or in times past where the Consensus was less rigid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T00:10:15-07:00","id":1219548,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that adding a human disguise should make quite a few bygones playable. It can be a merit for being or an enchanted item. Would be fitting with consensus too, as in many fiction legendary beings have human form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T00:20:35-07:00","id":1219550,"title":"","content":"I think that Revenants ( from most, if not all, Revenant Families ) could be good and interesting Consors of Mages. A good reason(s) and justification(s) in the Revenant's and Mage's backgrounds would be needed for this, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-17-2018, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T00:43:10-07:00","id":1219554,"title":"","content":"Sure. Same with eastern half-vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T07:01:03-07:00","id":1219617,"title":"","content":"Some mages are also vampire hunters. An independent Ghoul that hunts vampires for blood could use the help of a mage. A Consor relationship it's easy to imagine between such a pair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T08:32:10-07:00","id":1219659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1219550#post1219550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Revenants ( from most, if not all, Revenant Families ) could be good and interesting Consors of Mages. A good reason(s) and justification(s) in the Revenant's and Mage's backgrounds would be needed for this, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Revenants would show up as odd under Life 1, Spirit 1, Time 1 or Prime 1. It wouldn't be hard to justify a Progenitor discovering and studying Revenant families... however it would need a good backstory to explain one of them being an ally without this being deemed unmutual. Hermetics have their own links to Vampires, and some will have made a study of Ghouls. And remember that Revenants are themselves blessed with long lives and access to some supernatural lore. If I were a bored rich Grimaldi kid, going through high school for the 3rd time, I would make a habit of investigating the supernatural for fun, knowing that some Celerity/Fortitude and family connections can get me out of trouble. Given time and effort (they have plenty to spare) finding a sorcerer or Mage wouldn't be beyond belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:05:11-07:00","id":1220005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1219659#post1219659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermetics have their own links to Vampires, and some will have made a study of Ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are another possibility for who can be a Consor of a Mage. Perhaps especially fitting are Ghouls of Elder Vampires and Ghouls of Methuselah Vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1219659#post1219659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Revenants would show up as odd under Life 1, Spirit 1, Time 1 or Prime 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does slowed down aging or halted aging of any kind show up in Time 1 Magickal Senses ?<br /> And why Spirit 1 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-18-2018, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:43:10-07:00","id":1220018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1220005#post1220005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls are another possibility for who can be a Consor of a Mage. Perhaps especially fitting are Ghouls of Elder Vampires and Ghouls of Methuselah Vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does slowed down aging or halted aging of any kind show up in Time 1 Magickal Senses ?<br /> And why Spirit 1 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that anyone whose aging is slowed or halted will show up as strange under Time 1, although it would need many more successes than the others. I mean honestly I feel like Time 1 does the least cool things out of the level 1 spheres, so allowing a Mage to determine that someone is a Vampire or Ghoul based on their pattern being &quot;a still point in time&quot; isn't that crazy. I mean Time 1 can sense the use of Celerity and Temporis, and can see if someone has used Time magick in recent history, so a person simply never aging (or at 1/4 of the rate) showing up clearly seems fair.<br /> <br /> Spirit 1 can show Auras, and Ghouls of all kinds have paler auras than normal humans.<br /> <br /> Life 1; Revenant physiology isn't normal.<br /> <br /> Prime 1; Revenants are chock full of delicious Tass, and will be roughly 2x as energetic as most humans (the normal 10 for a large animal, plus 10 points of Vitae).<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Mind 1 could quite reasonably sense the Beast lurking just behind a Ghoul's surface thoughts, especially if they were angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T03:12:41-07:00","id":1220218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1220018#post1220018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life 1; Revenant physiology isn't normal.<br /> <br /> Prime 1; Revenants are chock full of delicious Tass, and will be roughly 2x as energetic as most humans (the normal 10 for a large animal, plus 10 points of Vitae).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How many Mages - and what kinds of Mages, and how skilled - would be able to identify Revenants with Life 1 or Prime 1, you think ? I think that relatively few Mages would have this capability with her or his Magick ( less than 15 % of Mages ) ; and it would be Spells and Rotes that would be difficult to learn, and difficult to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T04:07:25-07:00","id":1220224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1220218#post1220218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Mages - and what kinds of Mages, and how skilled - would be able to identify Revenants with Life 1 or Prime 1, you think ? I think that relatively few Mages would have this capability with her or his Magick ( less than 15 % of Mages ) ; and it would be Spells and Rotes that would be difficult to learn, and difficult to cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it depends on the context. A lot of this is situational; most Mages don't scan random humans for information all of the time. But if you notice something odd about a person, you might be inclined to examine them carefully. Life would be more reliable if the Revenant were healing, or Blood Pumped. Prime would be more reliable if they had recently spent some Vitae. And the most reliable way of sensing them would be to simply mix together some level 1 effects.<br /> <br /> &quot;I open my mind up and try to dissect their form. Life 1 to examine their physiology, Mind 1 to bring out their surface thoughts, Prime 1 to slice in and examine their energy and aura...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:36:03-07:00","id":1220336,"title":"","content":"Oh the signs should be fairly trivial to detect. 1 success at common sensory magick. To be able to interpret what those signs mean, on the other hand, would be rather difficult, and a matter of Lore.<br /> <br /> Mages would instantly know that the Revenant &quot;it's not right&quot;, and with study and further successes they could pry why. Mages that know about vampires will think he's a Ghoul (much like a vampire with Auspex would) at first glance. Only mages that know about Revenants (Like Tal'mahe'Ra mages, for instance) would trully understand the signs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T02:19:22-07:00","id":1220473,"title":"","content":"I think that some Kinfolk of Fera could make good and interesting Consors of Mages ; maybe Kinfolk of some Fera would particularly get along with specific kinds of Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-20-2018, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T22:54:37-07:00","id":1220732,"title":"","content":"this is all nice, but vampires/fera are already discussed in the books. what about something else? a hell hound, an exiled demon, beast from Pangea, elemental-claimed, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T03:30:59-07:00","id":1220774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1220732#post1220732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is all nice, but vampires/fera are already discussed in the books. what about something else? a hell hound, an exiled demon, beast from Pangea, elemental-claimed, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A hell hound or an ancient beast works as a Familiar. That background is a great way of reflecting really varied supernatural allies, over a wide power range (1 is a glorified pet with mechanical advantages, 5 is probably more powerful than you in many ways) and a wide range of origins. The background can capture a cloned manservant for a Technocrat, or a robot cat, or a regular cat, or your Kinfolk Lupus half-sister, or a friendly &quot;alien&quot; you met in an alternate dimension...<br /> <br /> These pets (?) cost 1 Quintessence per week per dot in the Background, and can absorb Paradox up to their level x 5, and shed one dot of Paradox per week. They double as a helper, ally etc. but naturally the energy cost balances this out. So if you're an eccentric Etherite your Level 5 Familiar could be a Cyber-Tooth Tiger, a cyborg you and your mentor developed from DNA taken from fossilized saber-tooth remains... and of course that's going to be a dangerous pet you can unleash whenever you like. But 5 points of Quintessence each week is a LOT.<br /> <br /> One thing I like in Mage is capturing many many things in a single neat mechanic. A sanctum can be anything from a dojo to a lab to an office to a surgical theater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-21-2018, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:51:06-07:00","id":1221783,"title":"","content":"What happens when you run out of quintessence ? Do they disappear? Leave you ? Break ?<br /> I woukd totally like a standby mode for a construct, or a spirit form for mystic creatures","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:18:27-07:00","id":1221792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RandyRando</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1221783#post1221783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when you run out of quintessence ? Do they disappear? Leave you ? Break ?<br /> I woukd totally like a standby mode for a construct, or a spirit form for mystic creatures</div> </div> </div> </div>The Background says that if you don't give them their weekly Quintessence (which could be given through affection for a cat, or special batteries for a robot, a specialized waveform generator for the alien you picked up in Otherspace, or through intimate contact if they're human-like) they will leave. Now while such behaviour suits a cat or a spirit, I really don't see a robot dog suddenly running away b/c you didn't change the batteries. Technically speaking the Background should be lost forever if you fail to feed them, regardless of in-universe justification for getting it back... this is meant to balance out how much Paradox you can get rid of, and how good their traits are, and how obedient they are. A Level 5 Familiar has really incredible traits and is Mentor, Ally and Retainer all in one in some ways.<br /> <br /> In all honesty I would allow a Player to recover their powered down robot, or hop into the Umbra to find their spirit friend. Some mental or social rolls might be needed to justify the recovery.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm sorry for not feeding you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I *was* trapped in a Paradox Realm. Listen, I promise it won't happen again.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll get you a new... box? Or bag? Anything you want.&quot;<br /> <br /> (From across the street, some people sipping tea outside a cafe watch as this strange homeless (?) person continues talking loudly to a stray cat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:25:08-07:00","id":1221794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1221792#post1221792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Background says that if you don't give them their weekly Quintessence (which could be given through affection for a cat, or special batteries for a robot, a specialized waveform generator for the alien you picked up in Otherspace, or through intimate contact if they're human-like) they will leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it would be possible that a Familiar in such a situation that they don't get Quitessence from the Mage that they are involved with would learn / become able to - in one of the many varied ways that I think it can be learned by a Familiar - gather or create Quintessence through her or his effort, without any need for the Mage being directly or indirectly involved in this. I think that all Familiars are capable of this ( maybe there are very rare exceptions ; but I think that in the end there are no exceptions to this ) .<br /> Do you think that this is possible in regards to Familiars and them having access to Quintessence - and being able to use it - through their own actions ; without the Mage that they are involved directly or indirectly doing anything in regards to this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-05-2018, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:40:20-07:00","id":1221799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1221794#post1221794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it would be possible that a Familiar in such a situation that they don't get Quitessence from the Mage that they are involved with would learn / become able to - in one of the many varied ways that I think it can be learned by a Familiar - gather or create Quintessence through her or his effort, without any need for the Mage being directly or indirectly involved in this. I think that all Familiars are capable of this ( maybe there are very rare exceptions ; but I think that in the end there are no exceptions to this ) .<br /> Do you think that this is possible in regards to Familiars and them having access to Quintessence - and being able to use it - through their own actions ; without the Mage that they are involved directly or indirectly doing anything in regards to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if you don't give any Quintessence (a gulp of your blood) to your Familiar (the genetically enhanced vampire bat you developed as a proof of concept), then it's perfectly fair that a Storyteller could &quot;punish&quot; (not fond of that word, but I think it conveys the right idea) you by having the bat look elsewhere for its meals. And since it's a Familiar, and strengthened by years of drinking your delicious Quintessence, it's going to be capable of lethally harming people and animals. First it might be every single lab animal in your Base/Chantry, all drained of blood. Then maybe someone associated with the Base/Chantry will disappear. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And if you're dealing with a robot, it might tie itself into the mains to try and access the energy it needs, causing a huge blackout. That sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:08:32-07:00","id":1221812,"title":"","content":"Familiars, without any special power, can still feed themselves out of Tass.<br /> <br /> If you don't feed him, you may find your lvl 5 robot familiar has taken control of your Node/Sanctum and isn't willing to let you in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T10:33:55-07:00","id":1222075,"title":"","content":"( false post please ignore.. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","user":"RandyRando","date":". 05-25-2018, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T03:27:34-07:00","id":1222194,"title":"","content":"aand that's exactly why I wanted something different the familiar background.<br /> Let's for example take a Golem from middle ages mage. It has ~8 strength and stamina, is utterly loyal and can be powered down safely to save on quintessence. of course it doesn't provide other familiar benefits, it's like a HIT mark for traditions. That's what I had in mind, how much would it cost in background points to gain such minions. For an example, what if your mage bought a high quality zombies, saturated with preservatives and equipped with armor, Ak-47s and prime2 machetes. how much a group of say 12 would cost in background points. No other benefits included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T05:43:49-07:00","id":1222219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219327-supernatural-consors-retainers?p=1222194#post1222194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aand that's exactly why I wanted something different the familiar background.<br /> Let's for example take a Golem from middle ages mage. It has ~8 strength and stamina, is utterly loyal and can be powered down safely to save on quintessence. of course it doesn't provide other familiar benefits, it's like a HIT mark for traditions. That's what I had in mind, how much would it cost in background points to gain such minions. For an example, what if your mage bought a high quality zombies, saturated with preservatives and equipped with armor, Ak-47s and prime2 machetes. how much a group of say 12 would cost in background points. No other benefits included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask your ST?<br /> <br /> If you put enough background points into Retainer, then you can get a single Retainer who has equivalent starting dots to a PC at character generation. So hypothetically 5 background points gets you your Golem, since you're just shifting points from Knowledges and Mental Attributes using some extra Strength, Stamina and Brawl... as for 12 mega-AK-47 military grade machete-wielding malevolent zombies... I think that lies beyond starting Backgrounds in most games. If the ST agrees to it it will likely take more than 5 points. Probably more suited to a game where the Mages are already established and advanced Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T02:20:04-07:00","id":1224919,"title":"","content":"Okay. found it. Gene-engineered creatures background from Progenitors Revised. Pretty much the same, but for traditions. sounds pretty much what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}